From 35ccd09ff54ebe2ec6dfea06211796abbd4d5426 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:03:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] feat(multiaxis): start and exit picks for the 5-axis
 contour

The 5-Axis Contour takes a start point and an exit point
(PickCapability::Ring). Each closed waterline ring is re-sequenced to
begin at its point nearest the start pick, and after its lap runs on to
its point nearest the exit pick. The cut order and geometry do not
change; the stamp, the shank dodge and the centre-cutting guard judge
the seated path. A pick far from every ring, a ladder with no closed
ring, and a blocked plunge or retract column at the pick are refused by
name. A path without a pick is byte-identical.

Refs #3330

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
