From 294362eb7de84f34416e9ab2ea4c8587aa6e6a5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:47:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] test(motion): contour5d seam pins sample each cut and pin
 the exit column law

The exit pins checked only move end points, so a chord across a ring
passed. Each level cut is now sampled every 0.25 mm against the automatic
ladder. The exit retract column law gets a pin on the untrimmed ladder
(a canopy above the exit point). nearest states a foot at a segment end
as the start of the next segment, so the run-on never re-traces a lap
for the closing vertex. The #3330 pins move to multiaxis/seam.rs to keep
multiaxis.rs under 400 lines.

Refs #3330

